{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLGGzZHSnq3bL5kzvGLr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #223 as **done**: it goes to the engineer for a plan, and the engineer worker will implement it. The routing file is at `.ard/223/triage-lead.md`.\n\n**What the bug is:** the approval gate can say an issue is ready for approval when it has no `plan.md`. That happens when someone removes the request label by hand, because the gate can't tell that apart from the engineer finishing. The fix is to make the gate refuse in that case, set `ard:needs-human` and post one comment saying why.\n\n**Why only the engineer:** the gate logic is in `internal/triage/fanin.go`, with tests in `internal/triage/fanin_test.go`, plus an edit to the triage section of `docs/proposal.md`. That's one package and one doc, so it doesn't need wider planning. The only other triage role in this repository is me, so there was nothing else to route to. The eng-review reviewer has no rule that would skip it, so it will run on the pull request anyway.\n\n**Open issue for a maintainer:** `docs/runbooks/gate-2.md` also describes the ready-for-approval step and may need a matching note. The issue doesn't ask for that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":524,"cache_read_input_tokens":11263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":524},"output_tokens":381,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1650057-050d-4a76-9dfa-0e22ca506fe1","uuid":"6b449275-48f3-45f9-80d1-a106b639a5eb","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:36:01.523Z","request_id":"req_011ChLGGzR6yZSwFqPNTk8rc"}
